From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:27:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] radv/ps5: fence status without the clock, and waits that
 sleep less

vkGetFenceStatus waits with an absolute timeout of 0, and every one that
found its fence not yet signalled read the monotonic clock to learn so, a
system call on the console. Cemu asks after every submission and on every
occlusion query update. A zero timeout now returns VK_TIMEOUT without it.

A wait that outlasts its 1.5 ms spin slept a millisecond between looks at
the marker, so it woke up to a millisecond after the GPU got there. The
flip thread waits that way for each frame before submitting its flip, and
Cemu waits that way for the previous frame at every swap: a frame done
just before a vblank could miss it. The sleeps are now 200 us.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VwQbTVomEg8vnnGcSRXLMp
---
 src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_sync.c   | 6 ++++++
 src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_winsys.c | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_sync.c b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_sync.c
index a01b3bc..6b7717d 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_sync.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_sync.c
@@ -140,6 +140,12 @@ radv_ps5_sync_wait_many(struct vk_device *device, uint32_t wait_count, const str
          mtx_unlock(&queue->sync_lock);
          return VK_SUCCESS;
       }
+      /* A status query (vkGetFenceStatus) asks with no time at all: it
+       * needs no clock, which is a system call on the console. */
+      if (abs_timeout_ns == 0) {
+         mtx_unlock(&queue->sync_lock);
+         return VK_TIMEOUT;
+      }
       const uint64_t now = os_time_get_nano();
       if (now >= abs_timeout_ns) {
          mtx_unlock(&queue->sync_lock);
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_winsys.c b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_winsys.c
index 6319a33..1be1645 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_winsys.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_winsys.c
@@ -87,6 +87,11 @@ radv_ps5_queue_poll(struct radv_ps5_queue *queue)
 /* Before sleeping, the marker is checked in a loop for this long: most waits
  * end well inside a millisecond (PS5_Vulkan R36). */
 #define RADV_PS5_SPIN_NS UINT64_C(1500000)
+/* After that, the marker is checked between sleeps this long. A wait wakes up
+ * to this late after the GPU reaches it, and the flip thread waits like this
+ * for each frame before its flip: a millisecond could miss the vblank a frame
+ * finished in time for. */
+#define RADV_PS5_SLEEP_US 200
 
 bool
 radv_ps5_queue_wait_seq(struct radv_ps5_queue *queue, uint64_t seq, uint64_t abs_timeout_ns)
@@ -116,7 +121,7 @@ radv_ps5_queue_wait_seq(struct radv_ps5_queue *queue, uint64_t seq, uint64_t abs
       if (now < spin_until)
          __builtin_ia32_pause();
       else
-         radv_ps5_sleep_us(1000);
+         radv_ps5_sleep_us(RADV_PS5_SLEEP_US);
    }
 }
 
